WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.880
Welcome to the lam rim (LAM RIM) retreat--the Steps of the Path to Liberation.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:34.590
I'd like to welcome Stanley Chen my translator, thank you for coming.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:39.397
And thank you for translating over and over.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:44.640
So as you probably know, this is our 35th Steps to the Path retreat,

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:54.600
and we are going through one of the greatest books,

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:00.020
in my opinion, ever written in this world.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.900
It's called "A Gift of Liberation Put in Your Hand,"

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:19.360
and it's a beautiful idea that if you study this book, and if you read this book,

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:33.860
then it's like somebody just coming and giving you freedom--liberation.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:39.480
So, this time we're going to be doing this retreat at home

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.200
because of the virus situation around the world,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:51.260
and I think it might even be better.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:02:00.460
Each day we're going to do about half an hour of filming,

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.980
and it will go for 25 days.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:17.960
And I think it'll be a great format for all of us, and we'll also be doing meditations together during that time.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:25.700
Each segment, each day, is going to have its own name

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:31.760
and each segment will have its own ideas behind it.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:41.200
And each segment has its own main image or picture.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:54.200
So, what you see here in the picture are steps going into the sky and there's a door in the sky.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:01.080
And that's the meaning of the word lam rim.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:12.300
I like to think of it like when you buy a piece of furniture from Ikea.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:21.920
You get a paper and it says: first do this, then do that, then do that.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:27.880
And you don't have to think too much;

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:33.600
you just do the first thing. Hook these two things together,

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:40.640
then okay what's the second thing? It says, "screw the screw here,"

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:50.880
then you just ... it's for dummies, and you don't think about the chair you're making;

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:58.640
you just do those instructions one-by-one.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:06.820
I don't know about you, but I get scared when I buy that furniture that I have to put together.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:14.520
I look at all the papers and all the screws, and I think, "Oh, I'm going to fail!"

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.700
And in my long life what I learned is:

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:34.720
just shut up, open the box, get the instruction book; don't look at the whole thing,

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:41.140
don't look at all the parts, just look at the first sentence.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:50.780
Put this screw in this hole. And then I do that and I feel okay.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:05:03.560
Then I say, "Okay, I'm ready for the second one." And then, if I just take it piece-by-piece, step-by-step,

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:12.360
and I don't worry too much really about what I'm going get at the end,

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:21.640
then suddenly the last screw went in and suddenly I have a beautiful chair.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:29.840
My partner, Veronica, says, "Oh you're so smart!"

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:39.400
And actually I'm not smart, I'm stupid.  I just do one-by-one. So, lam rim is the same;

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:46.760
just do the steps, dummy, one-by-one.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:06:05.120
Then suddenly one day, you look down and you don't have a chair, you have a Buddha body. Then, like "Oh, I'm done!"

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:11.530
So, think like that. Just take the steps one-by-one.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:16.440
Enjoy each step. Focus on each step.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:22.200
And then by the end you're a Buddha and you didn't have to do anything.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:36.460
Okay, so we started these retreats in 2010--usually 7 to 10 days

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:46.560
and oftentimes we went to Diamond Mountain Retreat Center, and more recently to other countries.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:53.640
We have a very pleasant annual retreat in the summer in Guadalajara, Mexico,

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:09.100
and nowadays we have a special retreat in Bali each year around December.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:20.380
Jasmine Yao from Guangzhou and her team,

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:33.500
they have like 700 people come to a beautiful hotel and we enjoy swimming in the ocean.

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:47.300
So, we'll still be doing those retreats. If the virus has settled down by July, we'll see you in Mexico--

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:50.140
very beautiful place.

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:56.220
And then in December, we'll see you in in Bali.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:03.300
And in October, we'll do a special retreat at Diamond Mountain in Arizona, in America.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:15.360
So each time we do a retreat, at the beginning, I'd like to tell you how far

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:28.380
did we go, and  how far we have to go. And I can see from how fast we are going.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:34.849
And by the way, I am purposely not going fast.

00:08:36.979 --> 00:08:48.600
They say when you drink an old wine, I don't drink wine, but you should drink it slow

00:08:52.100 --> 00:09:01.220
enjoy the taste, swish it around in your mouth, and then swallow.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:12.160
So, I want to study the steps of the path like that. We are going slow.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:26.240
In English, we say we are savoring the taste, we are enjoying the taste. We are stopping often, many times, to go deeper.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:33.900
And in some of these sessions, we'll just do a meditation the whole time.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:43.020
My dream is that these teachings on the steps to the path

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:53.560
the total plan is going to take 23 years. We've already finished 10 years,

00:09:53.560 --> 00:10:07.452
and my total plan is 13 more years. If we go on schedule we will finish in 2039

00:10:07.452 --> 00:10:12.200
and I will be 87 years old.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:21.389
Stanley will be 20 I think. Just kidding!

00:10:21.389 --> 00:10:27.400
So, in my feeling, in my opinion,

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:34.760
I want these teachings to be part of your whole life;

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:44.780
so 23 years, it's a big part of anybody's adult life,

00:10:47.580 --> 00:11:02.980
and my dream is that you have this support in your life for 23 years. And every year, three or four times,

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:15.980
you'll have the opportunity to go to another retreat if you want in-person, but we also broadcast them for free.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:24.760
We might ask you to help with the cost of the airplane if you have to come there,

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:38.720
or the hotel cost, or the cost of these cameras and all of this equipment,

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:50.980
but there's no charge for the teaching. And so for 23 years, I want you to just enjoy

00:11:50.980 --> 00:12:01.660
these classes and I think it will be a foundation for your life.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:07.920
My teacher took 30 years. He taught it twice in 30 years.

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:15.880
And for me, it gave me a foundation for the happiness of my life.

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:32.300
Okay, it's the 35th retreat now; we'll finish this book after 50 retreats.

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:45.080
Then this book has a sister book, which is called "The Great Steps on the Path," by Je Tsongkapa;

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:54.420
actually that lam rim was written before this lam rim,

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:08.940
and when that steps to the path reached the last two of the six perfections,

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:19.140
which is meditation and emptiness, then Tsongkapa ... there's a story, he had trouble writing it.

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:30.740
And he started, but he wasn't doing a very good job. And then he prayed to Manjushri,

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:40.660
the Angel of wisdom, and then he was able to finish the

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:44.180
section about meditation and emptiness.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:14:00.720
And it's something like 200 pages--so for dessert, after we've finished the fifty retreats,

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:08.660
let's do another forty retreats about this great,

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:14.800
great presentation of meditation--how to meditate and how to see emptiness.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:33.120
So, that's our plan. Your life will go through many changes during this 33 years total.

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:39.406
Your life will go through many changes;

00:14:39.406 --> 00:14:45.260
sometimes you might be very interested in these retreats.

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:51.000
You will travel to Mexico, or to Bali, or America

00:14:51.000 --> 00:15:01.800
to see those retreats, and then sometimes your family life, or your business life,

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:08.500
or your personal emotions will change for a few years.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:24.060
And maybe you will just watch them on the video, or maybe you will decide you're too busy to watch them,

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:39.280
but our plan--ACI's plan--we will video everything. You'll have 33 years of videos,

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:47.780
and when you're ready, any time you want,  you can go on the ACI website

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:53.120
and you can you can access these videos.

00:15:56.340 --> 00:16:05.060
So don't don't worry too much about it.  If you feel very interested, then fly to where

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:14.149
the retreat is being held;  if you're busy, then watch it online.

00:16:14.149 --> 00:16:19.370
If you're super busy, save it for later,

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:31.620
but our commitment is that in your life you will have these many years of teachings.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:42.340
They will be ready for you anytime you're ready.  In my experience,

00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:51.680
when people get a serious illness like cancer,  or something happens big in their life,

00:16:51.680 --> 00:17:02.600
like their their husband or wife passes away,  then they need support and

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:08.020
these videos on the steps in the path,

00:17:08.569 --> 00:17:13.580
they will be waiting for you  when you're ready.

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:20.980
They'll be here and we make that commitment to you. Okay?

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:34.360
Alright, so let's talk about the big divisions, or the big parts, we've already finished in these last ten years.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:42.880
The steps of the path are divided into three big divisions.

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:46.933
The short name is kye bu chung (SKYES BU CHUNG),

00:17:46.933 --> 00:17:49.589
kye bu dring (SKYES BU ‘BRING),

00:17:49.589 --> 00:17:52.760
and sky bu chenpo (SKYES BU CHEN PO).

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:58.580
kye bu chung means

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:05.010
"the teachings for people of lowest capacity."

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:11.300
And the lowest capacity person in the lam rim

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:25.640
is somebody who's worried if they are going to go down after they die.

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:34.280
And right now, maybe you're not worried about it,  but if something happens to you--

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:43.020
if you get a serious disease, or you get into an accident of some kind,

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:48.420
it will become the most important thing in your life.

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:52.780
Like, "Where am I going after this?

00:18:54.600 --> 00:19:03.280
How can I get some insurance that I won't go down?"

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:10.360
So, that motivation, or that capacity,

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:13.800
literally it's called a "small person."

00:19:16.100 --> 00:19:19.616
Then a medium person ... and we finished that.

00:19:19.616 --> 00:19:22.980
And if you didn't hear those early retreats,

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:26.520
you can find them online.

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:32.500
We'll put up all the links for you.

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:47.940
The second big section is called "medium people." Medium motivation.

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:53.520
And these people are like ... "Even if I'm reborn, even if I don't go

00:19:53.520 --> 00:20:08.590
down as an animal, if I'm born as a human it's so much trouble.

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:13.160
I would like to reach Nirvana,

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:19.040
and then I don't have to go back to a life full of problems.

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:33.480
Getting older and older, my body falling apart, losing my family.

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:44.540
I don't even want to go through a human life again, I would like to find ..."

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:48.174
you can say a human life, but one ...

00:20:48.174 --> 00:20:52.760
we call it Arhat, or someone who reached Nirvana--

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:09.600
they will never again live a life with any trouble in it.

00:21:10.340 --> 00:21:16.360
And then the highest section of this teaching

00:21:16.360 --> 00:21:19.040
is a kye bu chenpo.

00:21:19.100 --> 00:21:29.060
These are called "great people," and their motivation is more complete.

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:33.860
They say, "even if I get out of all pain,

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:41.158
it wouldn't be very nice  if my family cannot come with me,

00:21:41.158 --> 00:21:43.520
and my friends can't come with me,

00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:54.680
and in fact all the people in the world.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:59.360
And all the people in the many worlds  of this universe."

00:22:01.070 --> 00:22:10.039
I was reading an article in a science magazine yesterday and they've located

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:19.460
thousands of stars that have planets.

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:28.540
And according to Buddha there are people  on some of those planets

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:34.820
and they are also going through the same trouble  that we go through.

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:42.980
So, part of being a bodhisattva,

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:47.640
you don't just think about your own family,

00:22:48.460 --> 00:22:53.660
and you don't just think about your own neighbours,

00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:58.560
you think about people all over the world.

00:22:58.560 --> 00:23:07.839
If you study this teaching, you also realize your neighbours

00:23:07.839 --> 00:23:11.860
include many other planets

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:19.629
and we have to take care of all of them.

00:23:19.629 --> 00:23:22.980
So, that's highest motivation.

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:30.399
Now, we are in the middle of the medium motivation right now

00:23:30.399 --> 00:23:35.840
after ten years, and that had two big parts.

00:23:39.260 --> 00:23:41.358
One is called tarpa dun nyer gyi lo kyepa

00:23:41.358 --> 00:23:43.360
(THAR PA DON GNYER GYI BLO BSKYED PA),

00:23:43.360 --> 00:23:44.940
which means to try to have the

00:23:44.950 --> 00:23:50.409
motivation to reach a life which has no pain."

00:23:56.270 --> 00:24:07.289
"How can I get to Nirvana,"  which is [speaks chinese].  And then the second big part of

00:24:07.289 --> 00:24:11.882
the medium person's motivation is:

00:24:11.882 --> 00:24:16.474
what's the path to get to Nirvana?

00:24:16.474 --> 00:24:26.059
And to study the path to get to Nirvana,  you have to study something else,

00:24:27.740 --> 00:24:30.993
which is called kun chung korway juk rim sampa

00:24:30.993 --> 00:24:33.947
(KUN ‘BYUNG ‘KHOR BA’I ‘JUG RIM BSAM PA),

00:24:33.947 --> 00:24:34.740
which means

00:24:34.740 --> 00:24:38.560
"how did I get in  mess in the first place?"

00:24:45.460 --> 00:24:52.420
That question,  "How did I get in this mess in the first place,"

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:55.500
it has three parts.

00:24:55.500 --> 00:25:01.616
First part: how did I start to have negative thoughts,

00:25:01.616 --> 00:25:05.580
like anger, or desire, or jealousy?

00:25:12.400 --> 00:25:19.705
Then secondly, when I have those negative thoughts,

00:25:19.705 --> 00:25:23.000
how do I collect karma?

00:25:24.560 --> 00:25:31.415
Then, because of that karma I'm going to go through death,

00:25:31.415 --> 00:25:36.260
and I will have to cross to another life.

00:25:38.220 --> 00:25:42.199
And then we explore what does it feel like to die,

00:25:42.199 --> 00:25:45.860
what does it feel like to go to the next life.

00:25:49.940 --> 00:25:55.320
And we're in the middle of that section.

00:25:55.320 --> 00:25:59.520
So, that's the end of the first segment.

00:26:00.780 --> 00:26:03.673
The first segment was called

00:26:03.673 --> 00:26:06.980
"where have the steps taken us?"

00:26:10.240 --> 00:26:15.300
And we came a long way in ten years,

00:26:15.620 --> 00:26:19.300
and now we are going to discuss

00:26:19.300 --> 00:26:21.254
how is it that we die,

00:26:21.254 --> 00:26:24.189
what happens to us after we die,

00:26:24.189 --> 00:26:26.940
how do we go to the next life.

00:26:31.740 --> 00:26:35.240
So we will see you next time in segment two.

00:26:37.160 --> 00:26:40.560
Thank you.

